# TASK MANAGEMENT API — AUTHENTICATION REGRESSION TESTS
# VS Code extension: REST Client (Huachao Mao)
#
# BEFORE RUNNING:
# 1. Start the backend: dotnet run --project .\TaskManagement.Api\ --launch-profile http
# 2. Confirm the URL below matches the "Now listening on" address.
# 3. Change @testEmail to a NEW email before repeating a full test run.
# 4. Click "Send Request" above each test, IN ORDER (particularly tests 01, 02, 09, 16, 20).
# 5. # @name signup and # @name login save the responses for subsequent bearer-token tests.
#
# IMPORTANT: This REST Client extension stores all the requests in one .http file,
# but does NOT offer an inbuilt one-click "run every request" feature.
#
# Expected HTTP codes appear above each test. A response does not automatically
# pass/fail by status; YOU must compare the actual status against the comment.
# Never commit real passwords or access tokens. These credentials are disposable.
#
# Designed for: POST /api/auth/signup, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me
# NOTE: /api/auth/test is intentionally NOT tested (it should be removed).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5005
@testEmail = testuser101@example.com
@testPassword = SecurePass@123

### TEST 01 — Signup, new user | EXPECT: 201 Created
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "REST Test User",
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### TEST 02 — Signup, duplicate email | EXPECT: 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate Account",
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "AnotherPass@123"
}

### TEST 03 — Signup, uppercase duplicate email | EXPECT: 409 Conflict
# This uses the uppercase form of the default @testEmail.
# If you change @testEmail, update this value to match its uppercase form.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate Uppercase Account",
  "email": "TESTUSER101@EXAMPLE.COM",
  "password": "AnotherPass@123"
}

### TEST 04 — Signup, missing name | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "missingname@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass@123"
}

### TEST 05 — Signup, invalid email | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "SecurePass@123"
}

### TEST 06 — Signup, missing password | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Missing Password",
  "email": "missingpassword@example.com"
}

### TEST 07 — Signup, empty body | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 0

### TEST 08 — Signup, whitespace-only name | TARGET: 400 Bad Request
# If 201 occurs, your name validation still has a gap; don't treat it as a pass.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "email": "whitespace-name@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass@123"
}

### TEST 09 — Login, valid credentials | EXPECT: 200 OK
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### TEST 10 — Login, incorrect password | EXPECT: 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword123"
}

### TEST 11 — Login, nonexistent user | EXPECT: 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "absent-user-98765@example.com",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### TEST 12 — Login, uppercase email | EXPECT: 200 OK
# If @testEmail changes, update this uppercase email too.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "TESTUSER101@EXAMPLE.COM",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### TEST 13 — Login, email with surrounding whitespace | VERIFY API POLICY
# Depending on model validation, this may be 400 or 200 after trimming.
# Choose a documented contract; it must not cause 500.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "  testuser101@example.com  ",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### TEST 14 — Login, empty password | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": ""
}

### TEST 15 — Login, missing email | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### TEST 16 — Protected endpoint, valid LOGIN JWT | EXPECT: 200 OK
# First send TEST 09 to populate the login response variable.
# Response should contain the correct userId, email, and name.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### TEST 17 — Protected endpoint, no JWT | EXPECT: 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### TEST 18 — Protected endpoint, invalid JWT | EXPECT: 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token

### TEST 19 — Protected endpoint, tampered JWT | EXPECT: 401 Unauthorized
# Paste a valid JWT from TEST 09 below and CHANGE ONE CHARACTER
# in the signature (final dot-separated segment) before sending.
# The placeholder request as written is invalid and should also return 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_TAMPERED_JWT_HERE


### TEST 21 — Expired JWT | EXPECT: 401 Unauthorized AFTER EXPIRY
# 1. Send TEST 09 to generate a fresh token.
# 2. Send TEST 16 immediately: should return 200.
# 3. Do NOT rerun TEST 09.
# 4. After expiresAtUtc (15 minutes), send this request: should return 401.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### TEST 22 — Wrong HTTP method | EXPECT: 405 Method Not Allowed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login

### TEST 23 — Malformed JSON | EXPECT: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser101@example.com",
  "password":
}

### TEST 24 — Unsupported media type | EXPECT: 415 Unsupported Media Type
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: text/plain

hello